WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.680
Wayne Gretzky — arguably the greatest
hockey player of all time — said he didn't

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.500
skate to the puck, but to where the puck
was going. Ice hockey is a fluid,

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.150
unpredictable game. He couldn't know how
the game would develop, so he practiced his

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.830
skating and his stick handling. Today's
labor market is like that. Every month,

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.090
millions of jobs are created and
eliminated. Technology is changing how

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:32.099
jobs are done at an even faster pace. The
skills of today can be obsolete tomorrow.

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:37.290
What's a human to do? Like Gretzky we
should all focus on the basics. First is

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:42.629
mastery of reading, writing, and math.
Second: technological literacy. We don't

00:00:42.629 --> 00:00:46.739
all need to be coders, but we have to be
able to understand and use data and

00:00:46.739 --> 00:00:51.809
software. Third, we need to develop our
most human qualities: creativity,

00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:57.570
intuition, and empathy. Don't fight the machines — transcend them. A dynamic, growing

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.980
economy creates new opportunities every
day, but just like Gretzky, we have to

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:06.240
have the skills to take advantage of
them and to skate to where the puck is going.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.780
What do you think makes for career
success? Let us know in our poll. Also, let

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:15.960
us know what other topics you'd like our
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:21.830
sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

